From: fivefold3 <332818675+fivefold3.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: spread the AHB data-path interrupts over the CPUs

The IPQ5332 requests its DP interrupts with the default affinity, so every
tx completion and rx ring is served on CPU0. Place them with the helper
the hybrid (QCN6432) path already uses (patch 320): tx completion ring N
on CPU N+1, rx ring N on CPU N, like the PPE does for its EDMA rings.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
@@ -885,8 +885,10 @@
 					       ath12k_ahb_ext_interrupt_handler,
 					       IRQF_TRIGGER_RISING,
 					       irq_name[irq_idx], irq_grp);
 			if (ret)
 				ath12k_warn(ab, "failed request_irq for %d\n", irq);
+			else
+				ath12k_ahb_dp_irq_set_affinity(ab, i, irq);
 		}
 	}

